    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are several differences between Parametric and Nonparametric Statistical Tests, for ex. Nonparametric Statistical Tests are less powerful than parametric tests. From your knowledge about the parametric tests, which statement can not be correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. They are more robust and flexible\nB. They are based on homogeneity of variance\nC. They are used for ordinal and nominal data\nD. They are less sensitive to outliers\nE. They do not assume an underlying population distribution\nF. They are based on Independence of Observations\nG. They are based on normal distribution\nH. They can be used when data is not normally distributed\nI. They are used when the sample size is small\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
