      "generated_answer": "The sensation of thirst is primarily triggered by osmoreceptors in the hypothalamus detecting increased blood osmolarity (concentration of solutes) and by baroreceptors sensing reduced blood volume. Therefore, a combination of high plasma osmolarity and low extracellular fluid volume is the strongest physiological stimulus for drinking.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
