    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following propositions is an immediate (one-step) consequence in PL of the given premises?\n(N ⊃ ~O) ⊃ (O ∨ Q)\nP ⊃ (N ⊃ ~O)\nN ⊃ P\n\nOptions: \nA. P\nB. N ⊃ ~O\nC. O ∨ Q\nD. ~P\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break it down:  \n\nWe have:  \n1. \\((N \\supset \\sim O) \\supset (O \\lor Q)\\)  \n2. \\(P \\supset (N \\supset \\sim O)\\)  \n3. \\(N \\supset P\\)  \n\nFrom (3) and (2), using hypothetical syllogism:  \n\\(N \\supset (N \\supset \\sim O)\\) is not directly useful, but from \\(N \\supset P\\) and \\(P \\supset (N \\supset \\sim O)\\) we can deduce \\(N \\supset (N \\supset \\sim O)\\) — still not immediate.  \n\nThe immediate consequence comes from (2) and (3) by modus ponens if we had \\(N\\), but we don’t. The only direct one-step inference possible from the premises as given is from (2) alone by simplification-style reasoning: if we assume \\(P\\), we get \\(N \\supset \\sim O\\), but no premise alone yields a single step except **B** via hypothetical syllogism on (3) and (2).  \n\nThe correct choice is:  \n\\[\n\\boxed{B}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
