      "generated_answer": "The number of apples (A) and oranges (O) must satisfy 23A + 10O = 653 with A > O. The only integer solution is A = 21 and O = 17. The cost price of an apple is ₹20 and an orange is ₹8, so total cost is 20×21 + 8×17 = ₹556, and total profit is ₹653 - ₹556 = ₹97. Profit percentage is (97/556)×100% ≈ 17.4%, which corresponds to option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
