    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The total number of subsets from the set \\(\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}\\) is \\(2^5 = 32\\). Subsets with 4 as the largest element must contain 4 and any combination of \\(\\{1, 2, 3\\}\\), giving \\(2^3 = 8\\); subsets with 5 as the largest element must contain 5 and any combination of \\(\\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}\\), giving \\(2^4 = 16\\). The favorable count is \\(8 + 16 = 24\\), so the probability is \\(24/32 = 3/4\\).\n\n\\boxed{C}",
