      "generated_answer": "Let’s break this down:  \n\n- Each prism alone is a triangular prism with **5 faces**: 2 triangular ends + 3 rectangular sides.  \n- When you attach three identical prisms along their rectangular faces, aligning them perfectly, some rectangular faces combine into larger co-planar faces.  \n- Visualizing: attaching them in a row will join the side rectangles so that the outer surface will have **2 triangular ends** (unchanged), plus the top and bottom large rectangles (each made of 3 small rectangles), plus the front and back exposed rectangles at the ends, giving a total of **6 faces** in the final solid.  \n\nSo the answer is:  \n\\[\n\\boxed{B}\n\\]",
