      "generated_answer": "Let \\( x \\) be the length of the longer piece after cutting.  \nThe square formed from it has side length \\( \\frac{x}{4} \\), so its area is \\( \\left( \\frac{x}{4} \\right)^2 \\).  \nWe need this area > 4 → \\( \\frac{x^2}{16} > 4 \\) → \\( x^2 > 64 \\) → \\( x > 8 \\).  \n\nSince the cut is arbitrary, \\( x \\) is uniformly distributed between 6 and 12 (the longer piece must be at least half the wire).  \nThe probability that \\( x > 8 \\) is \\( \\frac{12 - 8}{12 - 6} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3} \\).  \n\n\\boxed{B}",
