    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s go through it step-by-step.  \n\n- Total lagaan collected = ₹3,94,000  \n- Mutter paid = ₹480  \n- Lagaan is levied on 60% of cultivated land, meaning the tax base is **60% of cultivated land**.  \n\nThe fraction of total taxable land (the 60% part) that Mutter owns is:  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{480}{394000} = \\frac{48}{39400} \\approx 0.001218\n\\]\n\nTo express this as a percentage of total taxable land:  \n\\[\n\\text{Percentage} = \\frac{480}{394000} \\approx 0.001218\n\\]\n\nBut the question is about \"percentage of total land of Mutter over the total taxable land\":  \n\\[\n\\frac{480}{394000} \\approx 0.001218 \\quad \\text{(not matching options)}\n\\]\n\nThis suggests the \"60%\" factor might already be incorporated into the given taxable land definition, so in that case the correct ratio is simply:  \n\\[\n\\frac{480}{394000} \\times 100 = 0.1218\\%\n\\]\nAs a decimal: 0.001218, still not matching.\n\nRechecking: If the 60% is separate and Mutter’s \"total land\" is larger than taxable, then we would scale by \\( \\frac{1}{0.6} \\), giving:  \n\\[\n0.001218 \\div 0.6 \\approx 0.00203\n\\]\nThat as a decimal matches **0.20304%** — option E.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{E}\n\\]",
