    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Potential generated due to movement of freely diffusible ions across a semi-permeable membrane is calculated using:\n\nOptions: \nA. Nemst equation\nB. Gibbs equation\nC. Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation\nD. Fick principle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation calculates the membrane potential when multiple ions are freely diffusible across a semi-permeable membrane, accounting for their permeabilities and concentration gradients. The Nernst equation applies to a single ion at equilibrium, while the Gibbs equation relates to free energy and the Fick principle to diffusion rate. Since the question specifies \"freely diffusible ions\" (plural), the Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation is the correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
