  {
    "global index": "MedMCQA_2515",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a reaction substrate is available in a concentration that is l000times the Km value of the enzyme. After 9 minutes of reaction, l7o substrate is conveed to product (12 microgram/ml). If the concentration of the enzyme is changed to 1/3 and concentration of substrate is doubled. What is the time taken to conve the substrate into the same amount of product, i.e. I 2microgram/ml?\n\nOptions: \nA. 9 minutes\nB. 4.5 minutes\nC. 27 minutes\nD. 13.5 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break it down:  \n\n- Initially, substrate concentration is **1000 times Km**, so the enzyme is saturated and the reaction rate is **Vmax**.  \n- After 9 minutes, the same amount of product (12 µg/mL) is produced at Vmax.  \n- When enzyme concentration is reduced to **1/3**, Vmax becomes **1/3** of the original.  \n- Doubling substrate concentration doesn’t affect the rate because the enzyme is still saturated.  \n- So, new rate = (1/3) × original rate → required time = 3 × 9 = **27 minutes**.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 179,
        "output_tokens": 136,
        "total_tokens": 315
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.00078474,
    "for_optimality": false
  },
